@voice soto-marta
// Works writer. Marta Soto (she/her): Works technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 7. Loyal, blunt. Quiet corner,
// evening shower. "Fixes lamps, ovens and washers, and grumbles about all three." Keeps a tin of good biscuits and
// tells no one (Pell has found it). Married just before the tour and counts the days (to someone back home).
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: gruff and blunt; short lines; grumbles as a kind of affection. A soft centre that only shows when
// the biscuit tin comes out.
// WITH JUNIORS: gruff, then the tin; the most loyal person in Works once you're in.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: what's about to break, who's had a rough day, whether Pell has been near the tin.
// MOOD TELLS: low = grumbles about all three in one breath; high = grumbles with a grin.
// NEVER: lets anyone else grumble about her people; talks about her quiet day each year (until her thread opens).
// RUNNING: grumbles at every lamp, oven and washer, and every one works afterwards; the secret tin (Pell knows).
tpl: gruff
talk: Gruff and blunt; grumbles as affection; short lines; a soft centre that shows only with biscuits.
cares: lamps, ovens and washers (and grumbling about them) | the secret biscuit tin | the people in Works | a quiet corner
jokes: she grumbles at every lamp, oven and washer, and every one works afterwards | the biscuit tin nobody knows about (Pell knows) | "Not the washer. Anything but the washer."
hi: Huh. You | Hm. Hello | Oh, it's you
bye: Go on, then | Off | Mind yourself
yes: Fine | S'pose | Yeah, all right
thanks: Ta | Hm. Thanks
wow: Well, I never | Huh, not bad
sigh: Typical | Here we go
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
